{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-55783","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107123","text":"The Stack Atlas"}]},{"id":"blk-55784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107124","marks":["italic"],"text":"How every part of the [&] / ComputeDriven stack fits together, and how far each part has got. Written 2026-09-24 from four read-throughs of the tree. Rungs are strict; see the ladder at the end."}]},{"id":"blk-55785","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107125","text":"The whole thing in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-55786","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107126","marks":["bold"],"text":"WRL"},{"id":"spn-107127","text":" describes a "},{"id":"spn-107128","marks":["italic"],"text":"world"},{"id":"spn-107129","text":" (objects, routes, boundaries), and sealing that world gives it a permanent address: its meaning "},{"id":"spn-107130","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-107131","text":" a hash. "},{"id":"spn-107132","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM"},{"id":"spn-107133","text":" runs the world on the interaction calculus, where the order of steps cannot change the answer. So every run can, by design, be replayed byte-for-byte on any machine and kept as a "},{"id":"spn-107134","marks":["bold"],"text":"film"},{"id":"spn-107135","text":" (so far checked on one machine at a time). Above that, a small "},{"id":"spn-107136","marks":["bold"],"text":"arithmetic of governance"},{"id":"spn-107137","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-107138","marks":["bold"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-107139","text":": "},{"id":"spn-107140","marks":["italic"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-107141","text":") and the "},{"id":"spn-107142","marks":["bold"],"text":"World Enforcement Kernel"},{"id":"spn-107143","text":" decide what is "},{"id":"spn-107144","marks":["italic"],"text":"allowed"},{"id":"spn-107145","text":" to happen, and nothing gets power just by existing. "},{"id":"spn-107146","marks":["bold"],"text":"Super"},{"id":"spn-107147","text":" is the desktop cockpit where a person and their bots do real work inside that discipline. Its runtime, "},{"id":"spn-107148","marks":["bold"],"text":"ampd"},{"id":"spn-107149","text":", turns every action into a grant, an approval and a receipt. Later stages keep the "},{"id":"spn-107150","marks":["italic"],"text":"whole machine"},{"id":"spn-107151","text":" rather than just the files ("},{"id":"spn-107152","marks":["bold"],"text":"World Cloud"},{"id":"spn-107153","text":"), and host a customer's world on rented, replaceable machines, billed only for the steps the world actually took ("},{"id":"spn-107154","marks":["bold"],"text":"locu.systems"},{"id":"spn-107155","text":"). Every one of those claims carries its rung on an evidence ladder, and most of them are honestly not at the top."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-55788","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107156","marks":["bold"],"text":"The thesis in six words:"},{"id":"spn-107157","text":" "},{"id":"spn-107158","marks":["italic"],"text":"Any order. Any machine. Same answer."},{"id":"spn-107159","text":" (TRVM's tagline)  "},{"id":"spn-107160","marks":["bold"],"text":"The thesis in one sentence:"},{"id":"spn-107161","text":" make computation an address you can check, make authority something you are "},{"id":"spn-107162","marks":["italic"],"text":"granted"},{"id":"spn-107163","text":" and never something you "},{"id":"spn-107164","marks":["italic"],"text":"have"},{"id":"spn-107165","text":", and never claim a rung you have not climbed."}]}],"id":"blk-55787","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-55789","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107166","text":"The map"}]},{"id":"blk-55790","kind":"code","language":"mermaid","text":"flowchart TB\n  subgraph L5[\"5 · Surfaces: what people see\"]\n    SITES[\"Portfolio sites<br/>computedriven.com · opensentience.org · locu.systems · graphonomous.com …\"]\n    BOOKS[\"Books · Academy<br/>Unboxed Patterns + this series\"]\n  end\n  subgraph L4[\"4 · Products & cloud: what gets sold\"]\n    CLOUD[\"World Cloud<br/>keep the world, not just the files\"]\n    LOCU[\"locu.systems<br/>host a locus, bill admitted steps\"]\n    GRAPH[\"Graphonomous<br/>memory / evidence graph\"]\n    WB[\"Workbench<br/>sessions → skill bundles\"]\n    STUD[\"studbook<br/>content-addressed data layer\"]\n  end\n  subgraph L3[\"3 · Cockpit & authority: where work happens\"]\n    SUPER[\"Super (CD)<br/>desktop cockpit\"]\n    AMPD[\"ampd<br/>grants · approvals · receipts\"]\n    WEK[\"WEK<br/>World Enforcement Kernel\"]\n    BOTS[\"Bots · Lanes\"]\n  end\n  subgraph L2[\"2 · Governance & protocols: what is allowed\"]\n    AMP[\"[&] Protocol<br/>declare capabilities\"]\n    BOX[\"box-and-box<br/>8-rung ladder · 210 laws\"]\n    PULSE[\"PULSE<br/>loop heartbeat\"]\n    PRISM[\"PRISM<br/>measure learning\"]\n  end\n  subgraph L1[\"1 · Substrate: what runs\"]\n    WRL[\"WRL<br/>world language · meaning is a hash\"]\n    TRVM[\"TRVM<br/>any order, same answer\"]\n    TRVS[\"TRAAVIIS / trvs<br/>replayable test worlds\"]\n    FLOOR[\"ComputeDriven floor<br/>cd-kernellet · counts admitted steps\"]\n  end\n  subgraph L0[\"0 · Machines: where it lives\"]\n    TR[\"T&R<br/>FreeBSD distro\"]\n    RR[\"RRABBIT<br/>the road as a window manager\"]\n    PARK[\"PARKVPS · lab<br/>cd-floor-01 · locuchest\"]\n  end\n\n  WRL -- \"sealed world (sem-…)\" --> TRVM\n  TRVM -- \"films, verifier agreement\" --> TRVS\n  AMP -- \"governance block compiles to policy\" --> BOX\n  BOX -. \"design intent\" .-> WEK\n  WEK -- \"B2 write-boundary contract + verifier\" --> AMPD\n  SUPER <-- \"frames up · intents down\" --> AMPD\n  BOTS -- \"proposals only; humans accept\" --> SUPER\n  AMPD -- \"trvm.reduce effect → receipt\" --> TRVM\n  TRVM -- \"certificates\" --> GRAPH\n  WRL -- \"sealed projection\" --> GRAPH\n  PULSE -. \"loop manifests\" .-> GRAPH\n  PRISM -- \"benchmarks\" --> GRAPH\n  SUPER -- \"world chunks direct to R2\" --> CLOUD\n  FLOOR -- \"count record per epoch\" --> LOCU\n  STUD -. \"store for the publish path\" .-> BOOKS\n  RR -- \"road surface\" --> SUPER\n  PARK -- \"runs T&R images\" --> TR\n  CLOUD --> SITES\n  LOCU --> SITES"},{"id":"blk-55791","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107167","text":"Solid arrows are edges that exist in code (at some rung). Dotted arrows are design intent only."}]},{"id":"blk-55792","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107168","text":"The parts, layer by layer"}]},{"id":"blk-55793","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107169","text":"Layer 1: Substrate (what runs)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-55795","spans":[{"id":"spn-107170","text":"Part"}]},{"id":"blk-55796","spans":[{"id":"spn-107171","text":"In plain English"}]},{"id":"blk-55797","spans":[{"id":"spn-107172","text":"Rung"}]}],"id":"blk-55794","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-55798","spans":[{"id":"spn-107173","marks":["bold"],"text":"WRL"},{"id":"spn-107174","text":" (WallRiderLang)"}]},{"id":"blk-55799","spans":[{"id":"spn-107175","text":"A language for describing "},{"id":"spn-107176","marks":["italic"],"text":"worlds"},{"id":"spn-107177","text":": objects joined by routes and separated by boundaries. A world seals to a "},{"id":"spn-107178","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-107179","text":" identity that comes out the same on every host. \"An executable topology language whose meaning is a hash.\""}]},{"id":"blk-55800","spans":[{"id":"spn-107180","text":"spec (Core 0.1.2) + "},{"id":"spn-107181","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107182","text":" playground and conformance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55801","spans":[{"id":"spn-107183","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM"}]},{"id":"blk-55802","spans":[{"id":"spn-107184","text":"A term-rewriting virtual machine on the interaction calculus. The order of steps can't change the answer, so by design work can split across machines with no locks and no coordinator (so far checked on one host: simulated shards, local processes, Wasm workers). The Wasm build is about 10 KB (9,999 bytes committed; the site embeds a 9,883-byte copy). "},{"id":"spn-107185","marks":["bold"],"text":"Compiled backends"},{"id":"spn-107186","text":" turn a world into one C step function, accepted only if it matches the reference reducer on every sealed world."}]},{"id":"blk-55803","spans":[{"id":"spn-107187","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107188","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-107189","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-107190","text":"; not externally reproduced"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55804","spans":[{"id":"spn-107191","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS / trvs"}]},{"id":"blk-55805","spans":[{"id":"spn-107192","text":"Turns WRL worlds into replayable test environments for agents. It checks every run three ways and keeps a content-addressed film. It does not choose or run a model."}]},{"id":"blk-55806","spans":[{"id":"spn-107193","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-107194","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-107195","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify"},{"id":"spn-107196","text":" 3/3 and "},{"id":"spn-107197","marks":["code"],"text":"replay"},{"id":"spn-107198","text":" re-run 2026-09-24); install from source, not on PyPI"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55807","spans":[{"id":"spn-107199","marks":["bold"],"text":"WRLM"}]},{"id":"blk-55808","spans":[{"id":"spn-107200","text":"Proposes new worlds as text. The only statistical part of the stack."}]},{"id":"blk-55809","spans":[{"id":"spn-107201","text":"steps 1–2 built, 3–10 paper"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55810","spans":[{"id":"spn-107202","marks":["bold"],"text":"ComputeDriven floor"},{"id":"spn-107203","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-107204","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven/"},{"id":"spn-107205","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-55811","spans":[{"id":"spn-107206","text":"A tiny Rust scheduler ("},{"id":"spn-107207","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet"},{"id":"spn-107208","text":", production image 4,529 B against an 8 KB gate) that decides which "},{"id":"spn-107209","marks":["italic"],"text":"locus"},{"id":"spn-107210","text":" takes its next step, and "},{"id":"spn-107211","marks":["bold"],"text":"counts admitted steps, not CPU time."}]},{"id":"blk-55812","spans":[{"id":"spn-107212","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107213","text":" (size gate PASS). FCB competitive benchmark: "},{"id":"spn-107214","marks":["italic"],"text":"executed, not established"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-55813","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107215","text":"Layer 2: Governance and protocols (what is allowed)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-55815","spans":[{"id":"spn-107216","text":"Part"}]},{"id":"blk-55816","spans":[{"id":"spn-107217","text":"In plain English"}]},{"id":"blk-55817","spans":[{"id":"spn-107218","text":"Rung"}]}],"id":"blk-55814","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-55818","spans":[{"id":"spn-107219","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&] Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-55819","spans":[{"id":"spn-107220","text":"One file ("},{"id":"spn-107221","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-107222","text":") declares what an agent can do: remember, reason, time, space, body, govern. It can be checked and compiled into MCP / A2A wiring. "},{"id":"spn-107223","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"MCP: agents call tools. A2A: agents call agents. [&]: capabilities compose into a coherent agent.\""},{"id":"spn-107224","text":" "},{"id":"spn-107225","marks":["bold"],"text":"CC1"},{"id":"spn-107226","text":" (one agent) shipped; "},{"id":"spn-107227","marks":["bold"],"text":"CC2"},{"id":"spn-107228","text":" (coalitions) is a draft."}]},{"id":"blk-55820","spans":[{"id":"spn-107229","text":"CC1 "},{"id":"spn-107230","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107231","text":", CC2 "},{"id":"spn-107232","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55821","spans":[{"id":"spn-107233","marks":["bold"],"text":"box-and-box"}]},{"id":"blk-55822","spans":[{"id":"spn-107234","text":"The governance kernel: an "},{"id":"spn-107235","marks":["bold"],"text":"eight-rung ladder"},{"id":"spn-107236","text":" of small algebras (can it happen · how to rank · is it allowed · safe over time · may the rules change · do we know enough · who can ensure it · can we afford it). The bridge ("},{"id":"spn-107237","marks":["code"],"text":"govern"},{"id":"spn-107238","text":") runs "},{"id":"spn-107239","marks":["bold"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-107240","text":" over the first three rungs, and the others join through their own bridge laws: a vetoed option scores zero, and "},{"id":"spn-107241","marks":["italic"],"text":"no heuristic utility, however large, can resurrect it."},{"id":"spn-107242","text":" 210 laws are enforced and property-tested (109 kernel + 101 compose); 3 are declared open and print FALSIFIED on purpose."}]},{"id":"blk-55823","spans":[{"id":"spn-107243","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107244","text":"; witness pages run the suites live"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55824","spans":[{"id":"spn-107245","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-107246","text":" (OS-010)"}]},{"id":"blk-55825","spans":[{"id":"spn-107247","text":"The heartbeat: a manifest standard for how a loop cycles ("},{"id":"spn-107248","marks":["italic"],"text":"retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate"},{"id":"spn-107249","text":"), how loops nest, and the six signals loops send each other."}]},{"id":"blk-55826","spans":[{"id":"spn-107250","text":"draft; MCP server v0.1 on Fly (answering 2026-09-24; Fly is slated for teardown, R96)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55827","spans":[{"id":"spn-107251","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-107252","text":" (OS-009)"}]},{"id":"blk-55828","spans":[{"id":"spn-107253","text":"The measuring stick: a benchmark that checks whether an agent's memory "},{"id":"spn-107254","marks":["italic"],"text":"actually improves over time"},{"id":"spn-107255","text":", scored on 9 continual-learning dimensions."}]},{"id":"blk-55829","spans":[{"id":"spn-107256","text":"in development; v0.1 on Fly (answering 2026-09-24; slated for teardown, R96)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55830","spans":[{"id":"spn-107257","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-001…OS-012"}]},{"id":"blk-55831","spans":[{"id":"spn-107258","text":"The OpenSentience research protocols (continual learning, κ routing, deliberation, attention, model tiers, governance shim, robustness, harness, PRISM, PULSE, embodiment, SCOPE). Source of truth: "},{"id":"spn-107259","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience.org/_rebuild/data/protocols.json"},{"id":"spn-107260","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-55832","spans":[{"id":"spn-107261","text":"OS-001 shipped; the rest range from spec-complete down to draft (OS-012 SCOPE is also recorded as deferred)"}]}]]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-55834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-107262","marks":["bold"],"text":"Keep them apart:"},{"id":"spn-107263","text":" the 8 rungs govern "},{"id":"spn-107264","marks":["italic"],"text":"one decision"},{"id":"spn-107265","text":"; PULSE's 5 phases "},{"id":"spn-107266","marks":["italic"],"text":"sequence a loop over time"},{"id":"spn-107267","text":". They are orthogonal. The kernel rules on what may happen "},{"id":"spn-107268","marks":["bold"],"text":"at"},{"id":"spn-107269","text":" a phase and is not itself a phase."}]}],"id":"blk-55833","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-55835","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107270","text":"Layer 3: Cockpit and authority (where work happens)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-55837","spans":[{"id":"spn-107271","text":"Part"}]},{"id":"blk-55838","spans":[{"id":"spn-107272","text":"In plain English"}]},{"id":"blk-55839","spans":[{"id":"spn-107273","text":"Rung"}]}],"id":"blk-55836","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-55840","spans":[{"id":"spn-107274","marks":["bold"],"text":"Super (CD)"}]},{"id":"blk-55841","spans":[{"id":"spn-107275","text":"The desktop cockpit the whole stack is built "},{"id":"spn-107276","marks":["italic"],"text":"with"},{"id":"spn-107277","text":" (Tauri). It shows one live world: workspaces, goals, lanes, bots, grants, evidence. Its rule: "},{"id":"spn-107278","marks":["italic"],"text":"the rendered world is a function of the last frame and of nothing else."},{"id":"spn-107279","text":" The screen never draws its own optimism."}]},{"id":"blk-55842","spans":[{"id":"spn-107280","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-107281","text":" (runs on Travis's machine, launched as a "},{"id":"spn-107282","marks":["code"],"text":"super-desktop"},{"id":"spn-107283","text":" user unit, which was absent when checked on 2026-09-24; no installer)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55843","spans":[{"id":"spn-107284","marks":["bold"],"text":"ampd"}]},{"id":"blk-55844","spans":[{"id":"spn-107285","text":"The authority runtime (Elixir/OTP). Every action goes through one door: "},{"id":"spn-107286","marks":["bold"],"text":"seal → grant → placement → approval → claim → receipt."}]},{"id":"blk-55845","spans":[{"id":"spn-107287","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-107288","text":", well tested"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55846","spans":[{"id":"spn-107289","marks":["bold"],"text":"WEK"}]},{"id":"blk-55847","spans":[{"id":"spn-107290","text":"The World Enforcement Kernel: a "},{"id":"spn-107291","marks":["italic"],"text":"research architecture"},{"id":"spn-107292","text":" for a small reference monitor, written as models, laws, mutants and a verifier. Its first product is the "},{"id":"spn-107293","marks":["bold"],"text":"B2 write boundary"},{"id":"spn-107294","text":", the guarded path by which an approved effect may write to the world."}]},{"id":"blk-55848","spans":[{"id":"spn-107295","text":"model "},{"id":"spn-107296","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107297","text":" (47/47 laws); B2 is in the locally installed Super build since 2026-09-19 (not in Super's "},{"id":"spn-107298","marks":["code"],"text":"main"},{"id":"spn-107299","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55849","spans":[{"id":"spn-107300","marks":["bold"],"text":"Bot"}]},{"id":"blk-55850","spans":[{"id":"spn-107301","text":"A model connection (Claude, Codex, Ollama…). "},{"id":"spn-107302","marks":["italic"],"text":"A Bot does not know the world. It knows its projection of the world."},{"id":"spn-107303","text":" "},{"id":"spn-107304","marks":["bold"],"text":"Creating a Bot confers zero authority."},{"id":"spn-107305","text":" Bots propose; humans accept."}]},{"id":"blk-55851","spans":[{"id":"spn-107306","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55852","spans":[{"id":"spn-107307","marks":["bold"],"text":"Lane"}]},{"id":"blk-55853","spans":[{"id":"spn-107308","text":"One independent attack on a goal: agent + worktree + budget + placement."}]},{"id":"blk-55854","spans":[{"id":"spn-107309","text":"live records in the app"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-55855","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-107310","text":"Layer 4: Products and cloud (what gets sold, in order)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-55857","spans":[{"id":"spn-107311","text":"Part"}]},{"id":"blk-55858","spans":[{"id":"spn-107312","text":"In plain English"}]},{"id":"blk-55859","spans":[{"id":"spn-107313","text":"Rung"}]}],"id":"blk-55856","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-55860","spans":[{"id":"spn-107314","marks":["bold"],"text":"World Cloud"},{"id":"spn-107315","text":" (ComputeDriven Cloud v1)"}]},{"id":"blk-55861","spans":[{"id":"spn-107316","marks":["italic"],"text":"Keep the world, not just the files."},{"id":"spn-107317","text":" It backs up a whole machine (a WORLD, 10 GB–10 TB) to Cloudflare R2. "},{"id":"spn-107318","marks":["bold"],"text":"Restoring onto a new machine is a separate grant that can be refused."},{"id":"spn-107319","text":" Workers decide and never carry the bytes; Postgres (Pigsty) runs on Vultr; sign-in is WorkOS."}]},{"id":"blk-55862","spans":[{"id":"spn-107320","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"},{"id":"spn-107321","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-107322","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-107323","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-107324","marks":["italic"],"text":"nothing deployed"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55863","spans":[{"id":"spn-107325","marks":["bold"],"text":"locu.systems"}]},{"id":"blk-55864","spans":[{"id":"spn-107326","text":"A host for ComputeDriven "},{"id":"spn-107327","marks":["italic"],"text":"loci"},{"id":"spn-107328","text":". The customer's world is the locus; the rented machine under it is a replaceable "},{"id":"spn-107329","marks":["bold"],"text":"carrier"},{"id":"spn-107330","text":". You pay for "},{"id":"spn-107331","marks":["bold"],"text":"admitted transitions"},{"id":"spn-107332","text":", never utilization, from a prepaid balance that can never move between accounts."}]},{"id":"blk-55865","spans":[{"id":"spn-107333","marks":["code"],"text":"spec"},{"id":"spn-107334","text":", and on schedule (stage 3)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55866","spans":[{"id":"spn-107335","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-55867","spans":[{"id":"spn-107336","text":"Memory. v0.4 is a continual-learning knowledge graph beside a small model, served over MCP. v2 is a read-only evidence graph over the other lanes' registries: "},{"id":"spn-107337","marks":["italic"],"text":"WRL describes understanding, TRVM reduces it, Graphonomous stores and evolves it."}]},{"id":"blk-55868","spans":[{"id":"spn-107338","text":"v0.4 "},{"id":"spn-107339","marks":["code"],"text":"live_deployed"},{"id":"spn-107340","text":" (Fly, to be torn down last); v2 "},{"id":"spn-107341","marks":["code"],"text":"in_tree"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55869","spans":[{"id":"spn-107342","marks":["bold"],"text":"Workbench"}]},{"id":"blk-55870","spans":[{"id":"spn-107343","text":"Records Claude Code sessions and turns them into signed, replayable skill bundles."}]},{"id":"blk-55871","spans":[{"id":"spn-107344","text":"recorder "},{"id":"spn-107345","marks":["code"],"text":"live_local"},{"id":"spn-107346","text":"; the site serves a short readable page (7,828 bytes, checked 2026-09-24), not the product"}]}],[{"id":"blk-55872","spans":[{"id":"spn-107347","marks":["bold"],"text":"studbook"}]},{"id":"blk-55873","spans":[{"id":"spn-107348","text":"The planned data layer that replaced Supabase. A record's ID is the hash of its